# ============================================================
# BUILD SETTINGS THAT ARE PUBLIC ON PURPOSE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the bundle, so anything
# here ships in the page and is readable by anyone who views
# source. That is fine for the one value below and fine for
# nothing else: a real secret goes in .env.local, which is
# gitignored, or in the host's own environment settings.
#
# THE GOOGLE OAUTH CLIENT ID IS NOT A SECRET. It names the app
# to Google; what actually guards the account is the Authorised
# JavaScript origins list on the client itself, so a copy of this
# string is useless from any other domain. src/lib/drive.js says
# the same thing at more length.
#
# Client: "Filmmakers Studio - Drive (browser)" in Google Cloud
# project `filmstudio-495419`. Origins registered on it:
#   https://thefilmmakerstudio.vercel.app
#   http://localhost:5173   (npm run dev)
#   http://localhost:4173   (npm run preview)
# A new origin needs adding there or the token request is refused
# by Google before it reaches Drive.
#
# Vercel builds from git, so committing this is what makes the
# deployed build Drive-capable. An environment variable set in the
# Vercel dashboard overrides it if you ever need a second client.
# ============================================================
# REPOINTED at the client Supabase signs in with, and that reversal is
# the whole reason one login can also connect Drive. Google records
# consent PER CLIENT ID: with Drive on a client of its own, granting
# drive.file at sign-in taught Google nothing about the Drive client,
# so GIS still had to raise a second consent popup. One consent means
# one client. The separate "Filmmakers Studio - Drive (browser)"
# client still exists and is now unused — left in place rather than
# deleted, because deleting a client is not reversible and nothing is
# pointing at it.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=186547817753-qkjgir1b1rd5b2lmcua8sq8ukukc42hq.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE — the project this build signs in to.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Both values are public. The anon key is a PUBLISHABLE key: what
# guards the database is the row-level policy set in
# supabase-schema.sql, not the secrecy of this string, and every
# Supabase web app ships it in the page. A service_role key is the
# opposite and must never appear here.
#
# They are a BUILD setting so that an ordinary visitor never has to
# know they exist. Before this, the app could not sign anybody in
# until somebody typed a project URL and a JWT into a modal — which
# is a chicken-and-egg for a hosted app: there is no account, and no
# admin, until the config exists. src/lib/cloud.js falls back to
# these and treats anything saved in localStorage as an override.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://conhlrulxfwkhsnymakz.supabase.co
# PASTE THE LEGACY ANON KEY HERE (the eyJhbGci… JWT badged `public`,
# NOT sb_publishable_… — supabase-js is pinned at 2.45.4 and predates
# that format). One line, no quotes.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZSIsInJlZiI6ImNvbmhscnVseGZ3a2hzbnltYWt6Iiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJpYXQiOjE3NzgwMDczODQsImV4cCI6MjA5MzU4MzM4NH0.jspvj56HdaZZ4vL6Rw_u0GgZ1Ae2lb5YsK8mpkOOYh4

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# WHO SEES THE ADMIN CONSOLE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated Google addresses. An email is not a secret and this
# is not a security boundary — the bundle is public and anyone can
# call the same functions from a console. It decides what is SHOWN.
# The thing that actually stops somebody reading or writing another
# account's rows is RLS, in the database.
#
# This is a BOOTSTRAP and should say so: the real tier already exists
# in the schema as account_members.role (owner/admin/member), but
# cloud.js makes no account-tier reads and no UI creates a member row
# — see open item 5 in CLAUDE.md. Replace this with that read when the
# Account panel lands.
# BOTH addresses, and the pair is the lesson. This was seeded with the
# address on the Google CLOUD account — the one that owns the OAuth
# client — and the app is signed into with a different Google account
# entirely, so isAdmin() was false for the only person who was ever
# meant to see the console. "The logged-in account is the admin" is not
# a thing a build setting can know; it has to be read off a real
# sign-in, which is the argument for replacing this with
# account_members.role rather than growing the list.
VITE_ADMIN_EMAILS=arunkumarmohanans@gmail.com,arunaaron85@gmail.com

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SITE GATE — the website is invite-only
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset (or anything but `off`) means ON: a visitor who is not through
# the invite gate sees only invite.html. That is the production value,
# and it is deliberately NOT set here so that nobody can turn it off by
# editing a line that ships. `VITE_SITE_GATE=off` exists for exactly
# one caller — `npm run build:open`, which `npm run verify` needs,
# because the gate measures every page signed out. See
# src/lib/sitegate.js and docs/GATE.md.
# VITE_SITE_GATE=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Razorpay — the PUBLIC key id only. docs/BILLING.md.
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Public, like the Supabase anon key: Checkout needs it in the page
# and Razorpay's own docs say to ship it. The KEY SECRET and the
# WEBHOOK SECRET never come near this repo — they are Supabase
# function secrets (`supabase secrets set`), read by rzp-order,
# rzp-verify and rzp-webhook, and nothing in the browser can see
# them. Blank means payments are OFF: every BUY renders disabled with
# a sentence saying so, the tiers still show, and the console still
# edits them. `rzp_test_…` for the test dashboard, `rzp_live_…` once
# KYC is through; both are just a label the server checks.
VITE_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_TlUnjCD0OCipuD
